Appendix O — Data Governance, Ethics, Dual-Use, and Legal Design

O.1 Purpose

To specify the governance of data, the ethics review process, the dual-use policy, and the legal interfaces of the Network.

O.2 Data Governance Principles

1. Provenance. Every datum carries a provenance hash and a source class.
2. Minimality. Only indicators needed for a declared purpose are collected.
3. Purpose limitation. Data collected for one pre-registered study is not silently reused for another.
4. Revocability. Contributors may revoke data under a declared procedure; downstream products are recalled and re-issued.
5. Sovereignty. Where national law constrains data movement, the affected data stays within the declared jurisdiction and only derived, privacy-protected aggregates cross borders.

O.3 Ethics Review

Every Mission Cell and every FCVN study undergoes ethics review addressing:

· human subjects (if any);
· privacy and DP budget adequacy;
· dual-use risk (O.4);
· potential misuse by state or corporate actors;
· whistleblower protection for internal dissent.

O.4 Dual-Use Policy

Dual-use findings are classified into three tiers:

Tier Description Handling
Green No foreseeable harmful application full publication
Amber Foreseeable harmful application under specific conditions delayed publication with declared review
Red Directly enabling severe harm internal-only; publication of the fact of restriction, not the content

The existence of Red-tier findings is disclosed; their content is not. This asymmetry is itself reviewed annually.

O.5 Legal Interfaces

The Network does not claim legal authority. It interfaces with:

· data-protection law (GDPR-equivalent regimes);
· export-control regimes;
· competition law;
· intellectual-property law;
· national-security review where applicable.

Where a legal constraint conflicts with a scientific obligation, the conflict is documented and the affected output is marked legally constrained.

O.6 Dissent and Whistleblower Protection

Internal dissent is recorded and preserved. Retaliation against dissenters is a governance breach under Appendix I. Whistleblower channels are independent of the Scientific Core.

O.7 Ethics of the Evidence–Scenario–Decision Separation

The Network produces evidence, scenarios, and decision support. It does not make decisions. This separation is an ethical commitment, not merely a procedural one: it prevents scientific authority from being converted into political authority by accretion.

